      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b9f6c965a3e1a116727dfa8|full_name}: Yes, improvements to the actual ranking system are also needed.\n\nThe intent here is simply that, if you're in a laggy server, and you see someone with a laggy avatar, setting an avatar block (or a full user block) is not ideal - you have no way of knowing when/if they switch to a more optimized avatar, and so you're likely to leave that block on longer than necessary. It also blocks more features than are necessary - if an avatar is slow only due to dynamic bones, then we should be able to just freeze those dynamic bones without blocking the avatar as a whole. Being able to set a \"minimum perf level\" - and adjusting that as necessary based on your framerate - provides a way of managing low framerates without permanently punishing people for having slightly suboptimal avatars.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
